WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:02.730
Aoi?

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:03.600
Subaru?!

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.650
What are you doing here, Aoi?

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.530
What are you doing here, Subaru?

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.000
There!

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.620
After-School Pleiades

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.790
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.250
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:14.630
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:20.180
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.440
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:32.480
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.280
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.370
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.450
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.170
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.040
We'll open the promised door

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.210
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.160
Good morning.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.620
Good morning.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.250
Aoi, that outfit looks good on you.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.500
Yours, too.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.210
You aren't getting on the bus?

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.090
Why? What about you?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.010
What?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.720
That's my...

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.270
This is my seat.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.060
No, it's mine.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:51.810
Oh, my...

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.320
We don't have enough desks.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.150
Where did they all go?

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.150
Itsuki...

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.150
Yes?

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.650
Why are you here?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.320
What's going on?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.780
We don't have enough desks.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.540
This is Aoi's seat, right?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.290
Huh? Isn't it Subaru's?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.830
Now that you mention it...

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.290
I think it was.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.750
Oh, there you are.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.750
Morning.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.000
Everyone? Why?

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.960
Because this is our class.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.720
But until yesterday...

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.640
Use this desk!

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.640
Where did you get that?!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.640
Song of the Traveling Stars

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.560
What are you all doing here?

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.820
Actually, we sort of had the same question...

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.020
The same question?

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:41.570
Yes, we haven't been together
from the start, either.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.200
Every time a new member has joined,
the same thing has happened.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.330
Yeah! With Itsuki carrying in
a desk from somewhere...

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.580
Not that part.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.370
Stop it!

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.040
A new member?

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.840
But it's different this time.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.670
Ah, jeez, how do I put it?

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.920
I'm taking roll.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.890
You five, return to your seats.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.180
Oh, okay.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.680
You all get along well.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.680
Now, let's begin our class.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.930
No one else notices.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.310
Everyone, open your textbooks to page 98.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.820
Today, we'll continue where we left off
last week in our study of proportionality.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.650
Okay, pay attention to the blackboard.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:28.120
I'll draw a graph to explain some terms
necessary for thinking in terms of proportions,

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.120
so watch closely.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.130
What's going on here?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.380
It is true that I summoned you all to help me,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:46.140
but my power should have only been
enough to summon one of you.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.390
What? Then which one of us did you summon?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.310
How would I know?

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.560
That's vague.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.560
Jeez, you all have it easy, you know.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.270
You have no idea how hard summoning help is!

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.280
And how would we know that?

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.110
Um, what is this?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.700
I told you yesterday. He's an alien.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.490
Yep, a Pleiadian.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.790
A-A real one?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.620
You've already seen a bunch of
strange things happen by now.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.670
What's surprising about an alien?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.290
I-Is that how it—

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.500
Space extends infinitely.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.090
The probability of an encounter
may be low, but it isn't nonexistent.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.130
R-Right.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.470
Well, I can't blame you for being bewildered.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:33.470
I wasn't certain before, but seeing you
and Aoi together confirms my suspicions.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.350
I know why you five were chosen, and why
you've all gathered at the same desk!

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.610
Huh?

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.110
The reason...

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.650
is because...

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.610
Hey, science rep, I need to prepare for
the next class, so come with me.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.280
Oh, coming!

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.370
Hey, you!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.500
Still, can't you do something about that outfit?

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.620
Is the alien invisible to other people?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.370
Don't you have anything white, at least?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:57.370
Yes.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.420
I do not.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:02.750
When we transform, we become
invisible to everyone else, too.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.750
Then how about wearing a
lab coat during science class?

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.590
Us, too?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.130
I shall consider it.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:10.640
So, what do we call an uneven coast like this?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.630
I was chosen?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.140
The story goes back seven years.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.770
Keep it short, or we'll run out of break time.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.940
Fine, then.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:23.400
To be brief, each of your
threads of fate seems to be

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.610
converging on this world right now.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.070
Threads of fate?

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.160
The five of us in one world?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.700
You made that too brief.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.120
Um, could you let me through?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.080
Oh.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.500
But Subaru and Aoi, haven't you
two noticed it, at least?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.040
That something is off, even though
you're sure you knew each other before?

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.590
I thought you left me behind
and went to another school!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.600
What are you saying?
You're the one who left me behind!

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.430
I believe the reason it turned out
this way has something to do with

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.850
the trouble my spaceship encountered.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:04.270
Yes, it's a story that goes back seven years!

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.490
Ah, we'll talk about that later.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.610
Let's go gather some fragments.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.820
Once we do that, our threads of fate
will return to normal, right?

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.740
Yes, that's true...

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.210
Today's been busy, huh?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.250
Usually, we try not to talk about
these things until after school.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.630
People would just think we're strange.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:29.380
I wish we had a quiet place where we could talk.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.100
Okay, I'll show you how it's done.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:40.850
I'm not really sure how I can teach
you how to ride a drive shaft...

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.230
But once you get it moving, it'll work out.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.110
O-Okay.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.400
There!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:57.790
Easy, right?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:58.540
Incredible.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.660
You're so good, it doesn't teach us anything.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.840
What's fundamental in driving
is your sense of balance.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.420
I can't balance that much on it!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.430
Stay calm.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.680
I don't know how that's helpful, but it's incredible.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.390
Jeez, you really think all that
nonsense is going to help her?

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.140
But...

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.520
I've never taught anyone before.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.150
Then you do it, Aoi.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.190
Above all, you just need practice.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.280
Accelerate more!

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.900
I-I am!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.360
Not enough!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.370
Imagine that you've become an angel.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.870
Flap those white wings on your back!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.080
A-An angel?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.290
That's a surprisingly girly thing to say!

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.130
Okay, let's fly.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:47.330
This is like driver's ed.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.960
Why am I with you?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.670
You don't want to be?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:54.380
It's not that. You should at least be in fron—

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.310
Well, shall we go, too?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:03.930
Huh?

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:04.390
Where?

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.150
I just had an idea.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:12.530
What, Hikaru and the others aren't coming?

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.450
Then we're gonna let 'er rip.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.780
Grit your teeth!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.670
Hey, hey, you two.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.510
Welcome back!

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.590
We went a bit too fast...

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.680
Wait, where have you been—

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:38.930
Here, refreshments.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.430
You two went pretty fast on that thing, right?

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.890
I figured you'd be hungry.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.430
How did you know?

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.560
Subaru, are you all right?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:50.440
Y-Yeah, though I think I feel a little sick...

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:51.400
Ah.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.610
You like this, right, Subaru?

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:54.570
Huh?

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:56.150
Oh?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:57.110
Was I wrong?

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.080
No!

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:03.910
Subaru?

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.410
I'm going to the bathroom!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.420
She isn't going to the bathroom.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:09.920
Huh?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.760
The key to the observatory...

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:25.720
I forgot to return it yesterday.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.290
Huh?

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:45.660
This is...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.080
You again?

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.790
Uh, hello.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:53.880
Over here.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:54.800
Huh?

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.100
Go on.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.450
Here.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.120
You forgot this.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.950
Ah, this is...

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:30.660
What's wrong?

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.210
Huh?

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:32.830
You don't seem happy.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.380
Well, this might not be any of use now.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.720
Hmm... Even though it's so pretty?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:40.510
Huh?

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:41.760
Y-Yes...

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.760
Um, do you want this?

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.390
Huh? Why? Are you giving it to me?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.980
Yeah, I don't need it anymore.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:53.850
Really?

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.650
You smiled.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:00.360
Huh?

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.280
You seemed sort of sad.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:22.380
I reunited with one of my friends after a long
time, but things aren't going very well...

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.630
Hmm...

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.050
It's not as if I didn't want to see her.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.890
I know I'm happy I got see her, but...

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:33.520
After not seeing her for so long,
it was difficult to talk to her?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.310
It's not that simple.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:38.110
So you didn't want her to change.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:38.520
Huh?

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:45.030
Do you dislike that someone you once knew has
become someone new without your knowing?

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.950
Or do you wish that <i>you</i> hadn't changed?

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.040
I don't know.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.750
Sorry. I don't really know, either.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.000
I don't understand what friends are.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:02.170
Hey...

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.300
Yes?

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.300
Why do you have horns, Subaru?

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.180
Huh?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:11.310
It always does this, no matter what I do!

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.020
I think it's cool.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.640
I don't know what you're talking about!

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.020
Hey...

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:18.900
What is it?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:24.650
Even if she wanted to change,
it's not that easy to do.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.860
How about you?

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.410
I couldn't.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.200
Maybe it's the same for your friend.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.750
Hey, in that case...

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.880
Why don't you just become friends?

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.880
I'm Minato.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.630
I'm Subaru.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.310
Aoi?

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.060
Subaru, where have you...

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:56.850
Aoi!

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.150
Fly with me again!

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.150
Hey...

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:11.160
When you knew me, what was I like?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.030
Huh?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.660
Never mind! You don't have to answer!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.870
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:22.170
<i>The Subaru that Aoi knows
is one that I don't know.</i>

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:27.720
You know, even if there's a lot I don't understand,

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.840
I'm glad I got to come to this world.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:34.180
But I guess saying that isn't nice to the alien.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.680
Well, that's its own thing.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:41.940
We gather fragments of his engine,
and it's fun using magic.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.440
There's no contradiction there.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.360
Aoi, what is that star?

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.450
Oh, that.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.740
I saw it above the clouds yesterday, too.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.990
There was never a star up there.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.160
Is it a supernova?

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.790
We can only see it when we use magic.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.960
It's the spaceship the president mentioned.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.290
That's it?

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.250
He said it orbits the sun like that.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.670
Hmm...

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.680
We used to watch the stars
like this together, didn't we?

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.220
Yeah.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:16.350
You remembered that I like strawberry milk.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:19.730
I was so happy, I cried a little.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.230
That doesn't mean you should
just run off like you did.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.150
Huh?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:30.240
You've always been a crybaby!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.450
Here we go!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.490
Faster!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:38.500
I can't!

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.500
We're not done yet!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.210
Wait, Aoi!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.050
She finally got her learner's after a week?

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.880
The basics of flight are speed and altitude.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.090
If you raise your altitude, your speed will drop.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:56.390
If you lower your altitude, your speed increases.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:57.350
Got it?

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.680
I-I think.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.560
Let's try it.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.980
Is this high enough, Aoi?

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.360
Not yet!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.740
Your speed drops, but your altitude increases.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.160
That's an Immelmann turn.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.740
I-Immelmann?

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.290
It looks like you're getting used to it.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.500
Y-Yeah, if I don't panic, I can manage.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.750
At a time like this?

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.090
Well, it's not like it'd only happen
when it's convenient for us.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.340
We're going on ahead.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.760
We'll be right there after a little break.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.100
Ah!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.350
Aoi, look.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:44.190
Is it a plane?

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:46.190
It looks like a variable star.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:49.070
What's that?

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:49.980
It's pretty.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:53.030
It's pretty fast. Twice as fast as usual.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:53.990
How can you tell?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.240
By redshift.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.370
Hmm...

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.780
Should we wait for Aoi and Subaru?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:01.870
It'll pass us by. We'll have to try on our own.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.960
Even if we can't degenerate it,
we might be able to slow it down.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.130
It's a bit scary, facing it head-on...

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:13.130
If we can't keep up on our drive shafts,
this is our only option.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:28.810
What's that?

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:32.940
It worked?

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.740
Something doesn't seem right...

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.200
Huh? Two?

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:42.790
They separated!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.790
Huh? It split into two.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.790
Let's go, Subaru.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:50.960
Is two at once even possible?

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:53.800
This is the first time...
But then again, everything is.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.340
Aoi, can you hear us?

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.800
What in the world's going on?

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:02.430
It looked like just one, but there were
actually two overlapping fragments.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:07.060
Right now, they've both been degenerated,
but they haven't completely stopped yet.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:11.480
Their relative gravity and centrifugal
force are in balance now.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:17.070
If either loses any force, they'll lose their
pull on each other, and both will spin off!

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.820
Meaning what?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:24.330
Meaning we have to stop both of
them at the exact same time.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.790
Subaru, the Immelmann turn, okay?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:28.710
Y-Yeah.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.140
What do we do?

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.730
Subaru, do you remember that song?

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:49.600
"Oh, see the red-eyed Scorpio..."

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.560
Huh? Oh, y-yeah.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.030
Yeah, that song. But before that...

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.870
Don't panic, Subaru. Let's stay calm.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.870
You, too, Aoi. Can you do it on your own?

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.080
Wha—

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.540
Well, you haven't been
able to do it yet, right?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.830
Don't take me for a fool!

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.210
You just got half-lucky yourself last time!

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.090
I can...

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.800
That's true.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.760
You really are the Subaru I know.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:24.720
You, too, Aoi.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.560
What are they planning?

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.280
<i>Oh, see the red-eyed Scorpio,</i>

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.030
<i>and the wide-spread wings of Aquila.</i>

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.200
<i>Oh, see the blue-eyed Canis Minor,</i>

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:48.580
<i>and the coiled-up Serpens,</i>

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:52.710
<i>and Orion singing far away.</i>

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.710
<i>Sending down the frost and dew.</i>

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.010
They did it!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:09.520
They were in perfect harmony.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.350
Huh?

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.020
The gravity between the
fragments hasn't dissipated?

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.150
That isn't what you told us earlier.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.530
These things happen.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.780
The centrifugal force is gone, so now
they're drawing each other in!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:24.740
They're going to collide!

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:28.950
Aoi, climb!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.410
Oh, yeah... Turn speed into altitude.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:47.550
Ah...

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:49.220
Again? What is it this time?

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.160
I told you, didn't I? These belong to me.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.990
What are you doing to Subaru?

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.490
You showed up again?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.290
Are you all right, Subaru?

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.370
Y-Yeah...

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.840
B-But the fragment...

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.590
You were waiting for us to capture them!

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:26.470
I can outwit you whenever,
wherever, and however.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:30.220
I'll come to claim the other soon enough, as well.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.980
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.980
I couldn't do it right...

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:44.820
Don't cry so much.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.860
If you do that, we can't be
as frustrated ourselves.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:52.870
You see, when I looked up

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.370
We're all frustrated.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:56.870
If he shows up again next time, I'll protect you.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:59.210
everyone was smiling at me

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:08.090
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.630
Okay.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:05.920
Well, at least we managed to get one fragment!

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.090
This hasn't been a total disappointment!

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:17.440
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:10.930
For tonight, let's head back and regroup.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.560
After all...

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.560
...my daily life...

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:15.600
Ta-da!

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:18.600
Starting today, this is our new room.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:27.030
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:24.110
This is what we were doing
while you two were training.

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:25.820
It was a lengthy battle.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:27.490
What do you mean?

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:28.910
"Can I fly?"

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:30.120
It was pretty tough to do.

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:32.870
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.870
Club Application

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.870
/ Name

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.870
/ Subject

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.870
Cosplay Research Club

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.870
The human desire to transform traces back several centuries to Western art and literature.

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.870
"Cosplay Research Club"?

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:38.920
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:34.700
Wait, you mean...

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:36.790
Yep, the five of us are the members.

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:38.920
And I'm the president.

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:48.130
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:42.000
But cosplay?

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:44.500
It isn't a complete lie, is it?

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:48.130
I didn't think we'd be able to get
a room so quickly, though...

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:51.760
I know, right? We got lucky.

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:53.310
"We have to catch them!"

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:57.480
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:55.350
Aoi, here.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:56.980
Oh, thanks.

00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:03.440
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:07.740
sometime after school

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:20.000
To Be Continued

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:31.630
You see, there's a reason you get born

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:37.020
Nobody knows what it is

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:46.730
But people still keep searching for a spell to prove their existence

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:55.700
Days with too much freedom might be too much to handle for some

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:53.070
...freedom...

00:23:55.700 --> 00:24:05.460
So they keep looking for the very thing to do

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:07.340
"It'll be fine!"

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:11.550
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:17.180
If you can't wait, let's go right away

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:26.860
Each star sticker you stick on will speed you up

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:31.490
"I want to embrace you!"

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:35.990
Of course you'll make it

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:41.330
because the promise between us

00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:46.040
is for all eternity after school

00:24:50.800 --> 00:24:53.720
The Cosplay Research Club
will now begin activities!

00:24:53.720 --> 00:24:55.260
What are we doing for activities?

00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:59.140
Huh? Why don't we just do it: cosplay!

00:24:59.140 --> 00:25:01.270
Next episode:
Five Cinderellas.

00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:04.310
I'm not going to do
anything embarrassing!
